doc: StatAltEquipCost is the battlefield static that grants the activated abilities it scopes an alternative cost (Kíli the Resourceful's "As long as you have an enduring story, you may pay {0} rather than pay the equip cost of the first equip ability you activate each turn"; S:Mode$ AlternativeCost | ValidSA$ Activated.Equip, gorge activate_static_altcost.go): the ability's Cost is the alternative (kop.Ability.Cost, CR 118.9: it replaces the printed one), Filter (no ValidCard$: the any-permanent one) matches the activated ability's source, StFlags kop.StReduceAny is a ValidPlayer$-less grant (every activator's; ValidPlayer$ You keeps the activator the static's controller) and Cond2 is the Condition$/CheckSVar$ gate read with the static's controller as "you" at the offer (the count gate is the zero count of the turn's first equip, which the activation's push already flips, so the charge carries the offer's choice on the stack entry and never re-reads it). The offer lists it as a second AkActivate action beside the printed cost, payable independently (altEquipTgt in the target field); the charge prices the alternative. Scoped to an Equip ability whose printed cost is mana plus kop.CostSorcery (gorge replaces the whole cost; a non-mana part needs a matchup refusal on cardset.AbReduceRefusal). Read live from the battlefield at the offer (kernel altEquipCost, legal.go), never stamped on the card.
